Z||000013||gold86||11-24-2001||10:30 PM||||I woudnt do it I just finnished my flushmount headlights like twenty min.ago  got them in even went as far as painting them to match car. went for a drive and hated it couldnt see worth a crap. So in the morning I am going to get out the dremmel and cut them out and put the old burnt up motors in and prop my lights up with the old chunks of wood. really disapointed cuz it looked outstanding||||reg||8
Z||000014||x-thumpr-x||11-24-2001||10:41 PM||||Hmm.. an idea to go with is use a smaller light in the pop-ups. Did a little research at the local crappy tire store and Dodges stealth (90-91) has a single HI/LOW headlight that is half the size and ours. Maybe with a light home mechanical applications, be able to use them instead. This way door comes up half the hieght it naturally does.<BR>I'd like to try to incorporate a pivot light as the corvettes (82-9?) with this light. Just don't have the time or facilaties to do it right now.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
