Z||000017||rogergarrison||11-25-2001||10:43 AM||||heres a new link to some of mine. i removed whole assby and made a plate that mounted to same studs. simple job then to mount the driving lites and wire to stock wiring. The cover just velcros on so ez to remove to clean or maintainence. they also stay on the car when i open the hood, cut out the corner. I cant find the Tornado headlites rite now, they must be in attic. If I remember rite, there 2 1/2 X 5 inches and the buckets are plastic. If I can find them you can have them for just the shipping. I also think there the same seal beams they use in full size chevy vans with dual headlite system.<BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=1234884&a=12102398" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=1234884&a=12102398</A> <P>theres some other albums there too you can browse thru||||reg||1
Z||000018||Monkeyman||11-25-2001||11:17 AM||||Thanx, Roger.  Those were the pics I remember seeing before.  I'll take the Toronado headlights whenever you find them.<P>Do you have a Mera or a kit?  Is the hood a stock Fiero hood or something else?  I thought you had cut out the lower and outside edged around your headlights, but they look too finished for that.  Can you email me any more detailed pics?  <P>Thanx.||||reg||1
Z||000019||theogre||11-25-2001||04:11 PM||||Driving lights are inteneded as a suplmental light for the high beams.<P>Fog lights are intended for just that, fog. they typically do little or nothing in clear weather.<P>For a better understanding of lights and limitations and how they are suposed to be used.... <P>NHTSA has an open RFC on their docket system that covers pending rules developement for auxilary lighting and aftermarket lamps to replace OE type headlamps. The Public Comment period closes on 12/1. Here's the press link <A HREF="http://www.nhtsa.gov/nhtsa/announce/press/pressdisplay.cfm?year=2001&filename=pr50-01.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.nhtsa.gov/nhtsa/announce/press/pressdisplay.cfm?year=2001&filename=pr50-0  1.html</A>  It tells you where to find the full text....<P>You can also read the lighting section in FMVSS. Section 106 or 108... It explains the current rules.<P>There's also a guy covering lighting on his site. <P>The links for the last two are in the safety link in my cave.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">    <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT><P>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 11-25-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 11-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||GTMike||11-25-2001||04:47 PM||||i think if you put two sets of driveing lights in the head light spot  and another set on the front, in the opening for air.  you could use one of the ones in the headlight spot and the ones in the lower spot for regular driving and when you need high beams turn on the other set that are on the headlight spot.  i think that combo would light up the road very well.||||reg||1
